---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

// Public, so Google's sign-in screen can link to it and anyone can read it
// before signing in. Built once as a plain HTML file, since it's the same for
// everyone. Update LAST_UPDATED whenever the text changes.
export const prerender = true;

const LAST_UPDATED = "4 October 2026";
const CONTACT_EMAIL = "info@helderbergpirates.co.za";
---

<Layout title="Privacy policy">
  <main class="page privacy">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">
      Clubhouse bookings app, Helderberg Pirates Baseball Club. Last updated{" "}
      {LAST_UPDATED}.
    </p>

    <p>
      This page explains what the clubhouse bookings app stores about the
      committee members who sign in to it, and why. The Helderberg Pirates
      Baseball Club ("the club") runs the app.
    </p>
    <p>
      It doesn't cover the clubhouse booking form. For questions about a
      booking, email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app stores about you</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your name and email address</strong>, from your Google account
        when you sign in. The app asks Google for nothing else: not your
        contacts, files or calendar.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What you're allowed to do</strong> in the app, such as viewing
        bookings or changing payment statuses. Club admins set this in the
        club's bookings spreadsheet.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What you change.</strong> When you change a booking or add a
        note, the app saves your email address and the time with it, so the
        committee can see who did what.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A sign-in cookie</strong> that keeps you signed in for 30 days,
        and two short-lived cookies used while you sign in, which expire after
        10 minutes. The app has no advertising or tracking cookies and no
        analytics.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        To check that you're a committee member who's allowed in, and what you
        may do.
      </li>
      <li>To keep a record of who changed what on each booking.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Nothing else. The club doesn't sell or share this information, or use it
      for marketing.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it's kept</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google</strong> handles signing in, and holds the club's
        bookings spreadsheet, which contains the list of app users and the
        record of changes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Netlify</strong> runs the app and stores sign-in sessions. Like
        most hosting companies, it may keep technical logs of visits, such as IP
        addresses, for a short time.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>Both companies may store data outside South Africa.</p>

    <h2>How long it's kept</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your sign-in session: 30 days, or until you sign out.</li>
      <li>
        Your place in the list of app users: until an admin removes you, for
        example when you leave the committee.
      </li>
      <li>
        Your email address on changes and notes: as long as the booking record
        is kept, which is 5 years.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the Protection of Personal Information Act (POPIA), you can ask the
      club:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>what it holds about you;</li>
      <li>to correct it;</li>
      <li>
        to delete it, or stop using it. Without your place in the list of app
        users, you can't sign in to the app.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. The club's
      Information Officer is the Chairperson.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you're not happy with the club's answer, you can complain to the
      Information Regulator at{" "}
      <a href="https://inforegulator.org.za" rel="noopener">
        inforegulator.org.za
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <p class="back">
      <a href="/login">Back to the app</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space);
    max-width: 40rem;
  }
  .privacy > * {
    margin: 0;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
  }
  ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
  .meta {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }
  a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }
  .back {
    margin-top: var(--space);
  }
</style>
